docs/input/prototype/prototype-extract.md-196-1. **"29 frames" vs. "32 states":** the prototype has 32 distinct navigable states, but the number of frames (29) suggests that some state families should be one screen with internal state, not separate routes (e.g., a single `ExportSheet` with a status enum instead of 5 routes). Consider this when designing navigation.
docs/input/prototype/prototype-extract.md:197:2. **Account deletion without a success screen:** both "Sair" and "Apagar tudo" return to the Biometria screen; there is no "account deleted" or "you signed out" screen.
docs/input/prototype/prototype-extract.md-198-3. **Login vs. sign-up:** the same screen toggled by a text link; the prototype shows no extra sign-up fields (e.g., password confirmation, name). Whether sign-up needs extra fields is a product decision not covered visually.
docs/input/prototype/prototype-extract.md-199-4. **Insertion modal when offline:** not represented.
docs/input/prototype/prototype-extract.md-200-5. **Switching tabs in the insertion modal:** opening the modal always resets every tab to `idle`/empty, but switching tabs *during* a modal session is not cleared automatically — the expected behavior (e.g., whether an ongoing recording is discarded on tab switch) is not defined by the prototype.
docs/input/prototype/prototype-extract.md-201-6. **Per-entry sync indicator:** the states "sincronizado / sincronizando / erro de sync" exist visually on the cards, but no explicit "retry sync" action is shown for the error state. The semantics of the badge are in `docs/input/backend/sync-badge.md`.
docs/input/prototype/prototype-extract.md-202-7. **Text search combined with filters:** the filter sheet and the text search are on the same screen, but the prototype does not show them acting together.
